[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Version=1.5
Name=Control Panel
GenericName=System Settings
Comment=Every desktop setting synui owns — appearance, glass, bar, audio, power, AI
# A compositor panel, not a program: synctl asks synui to open exactly what the
# keybind opens. StartupNotify is off because no window ever appears, so a
# startup spinner would spin until it timed out.
# ⚠ `control`, NOT `ctlpanel`. The action is named for what it opens, not for
# the file it lives in, and this entry shipped with the file's name from 392
# until 2026-08-20 — `synctl dispatch ctlpanel` reaches the unknown-action
# branch, which logs a line nobody reads and returns. The menu item existed,
# highlighted, and did nothing. tests/menu_apps.sh now checks every Exec here
# against the actions input.c actually implements.
Exec=synctl dispatch control
Icon=preferences-system
Terminal=false
StartupNotify=false
Categories=Settings;DesktopSettings;
Keywords=control;panel;settings;preferences;config;configure;desktop;appearance;system;
# ⛔ SYNUI ONLY. `synctl dispatch` talks to a running synui over its socket;
# under KDE or GNOME there is nothing listening and the entry would be a menu
# item that silently does nothing. Hidden there rather than shown and dead.
#
# ⚠ BOTH NAMES, and that is not belt-and-braces — the desktop identity is
# genuinely inconsistent today. A greetd login runs /usr/local/bin/synui-session,
# which exports XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=synui; a display-manager login reads
# /usr/share/wayland-sessions/synui.desktop, whose DesktopNames is SynapseOS —
# and a live ISO session gets synui from synui.service. Naming one of them hides
# these entries on the other login paths. See the portal config that was killed
# by the same split.
# ⚠ `desktop-file-validate` calls both names "unregistered" and wants an X-
# prefix. IGNORE IT — the prefix would BREAK this. Implementations compare
# OnlyShowIn literally against the entries in XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, so
# X-SynapseOS does not match SynapseOS and the entry would vanish everywhere.
# Every wlroots compositor that ships menu entries does the same thing. Nothing
# in this build runs the validator; runtime behaviour is the contract.
OnlyShowIn=synui;SynapseOS;
